A||||7||Fformula88||Rear decklid cables||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||12-18-2000||06:12 PM||||Has anyone had succes in replacing either of the cables that prevents the decklid from opening too far?  Mine are now both broken and just hanging there.  Looks like they have to be drilled out which would mean removal of the decklid.  I certainly do not want to do this.  Although having it open all the way up is great when I want to work on the engine, I am worried about the wind grabbing it and causing damage.  Thanks for your advice!||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-18-2000||08:17 PM||||It won't be easy but cut the eyes on the cable. A dremel tool comes to mind....<P>You might could make replacements of nylon webbing and use the old rivits like buttons. Another option if you could find it would be Kevlar cord. Either way, make an eye that just fits over the buttons and it should stay in place fine. <P>I'm not sure how much heat nylon would take. might not work for a V6.<P>If you used Kevlar with a crimp sleeve you could take a turn around the button before crimping. Then it should stay for good. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||12-18-2000||11:37 PM||||I've done some work on reproducing these. There are a few problems. The cables are expensive to have made and to get the best price you have to do a bunch in a batch. Making the ends plated steel instead of stainless steel drops the price a bunch. OEM ends are stainless. I have a design that will allow them to be replaced without removing the hinges from the car. I also have a design that is more OEM but requires them to be removed from the car and will cost more. If I see enough demand I'll look at continuing on with making them. The non stainless would be around $18 each. Maybe $22 each for the design that reqiures the hinges to be removed and looks close to OEM. To go to the stainless steel ends will almost double those prices. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||12-19-2000||01:52 AM||||ok, this is off topic but i gotta know. what exactly does OEM stand for??<P>don't laugh at me for not knowing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
