Z||000005||tgowens||12-19-2000||02:20 AM||||By the way, we have decklid hinges here at the shop........call us if you need them - 1-510-233-4376||||reg||1
Z||000006||deceler8||12-19-2000||09:11 AM||||Another option would be one of Rodney's strut kits. The strut only has so much travel so if properly installed it should eliminate the need for the cables.<P>Worked for me.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||12-19-2000||11:16 AM||||All sound like good ideas.  I had been working with some chains but they just were not working out too well.  I couldn't get them over the buttons to my satisfaction.<P>Rodney, a reproduction or even a close aproximation that could be installed without the removal of the hinges would be great.  I just don't want to rip everything apart to do this.  It works as it is, and is actually nice to have the extra room when working on the engine.  <P>theogre, I wouldn't try to use nylon under there on my v6.  I am almost certain the heat from the manifold and crossover pipe would destroy it (possibly start a fire!).  When closed, they would hang very close to that stuff.  But a kevar cord may work well.  Unfortunately, I have no idea where I would pick some up.  Never seen it for sale.  Any ideas?<p>[This message has been edited by Fformula88 (edited 12-19-2000).]||||reg||1
